(in-ns 'go.arbace.pytls) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "// Copyright 2009 The Go Authors. All rights reserved."] [2 1 "// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style"] [3 1 "// license that can be found in the LICENSE file."] [24 1 "// serverHandshakeState contains details of a server handshake in progress."] [25 1 "// It's discarded once the handshake has completed."] [42 1 "// serverHandshake performs a TLS handshake as a server."] [74 2 "// For an overview of TLS handshaking, see RFC 5246, Section 7.3."] [80 3 "// The client has included a session ticket and so we do an abbreviated handshake."] [101 3 "// The client didn't include a session ticket, or it wasn't"] [102 3 "// valid so we do a full handshake."] [106 46 "// arbace: or PSK"] [134 1 "// readClientHello reads a ClientHello message and selects the protocol version."] [136 2 "// clientHelloMsg is included in the transcript, but we haven't initialized"] [137 2 "// it yet. The respective handshake functions will record it themselves."] [148 2 "// ECH processing has to be done before we do any other negotiation based on"] [149 2 "// the contents of the client hello, since we may swap it out completely."] [181 3 "// RFC 8446 4.2.1 indicates when the supported_versions extension is not sent,"] [182 3 "// compatible servers MUST negotiate TLS 1.2 or earlier if supported, even"] [183 3 "// if the client legacy version is TLS 1.3 or later."] [184 3 "//"] [185 3 "// Since we reject empty extensionSupportedVersions in the client hello unmarshal"] [186 3 "// finding the supportedVersions empty indicates the extension was not present."] [200 2 "// This check reflects some odd specification implied behavior. Client-facing servers"] [201 2 "// are supposed to reject hellos with outer ECH and inner ECH that offers 1.2, but"] [202 2 "// backend servers are allowed to accept hellos with inner ECH that offer 1.2, since"] [203 2 "// they cannot expect client-facing servers to behave properly. Since we act as both"] [204 2 "// a client-facing and backend server, we only enforce 1.3 being negotiated if we"] [205 2 "// saw a hello with outer ECH first. The spec probably should've made this an error,"] [206 2 "// but it didn't, and this matches the boringssl behavior."] [222 2 "// We only support null compression, so check that the client offered it."] [237 2 "// Downgrade protection canaries. See RFC 8446, Section 4.1.3."] [275 3 "// arbace: a PSK server needs no certificate; only PSK suites can be chosen."] [298 3 "// Although omitting the ec_point_formats extension is permitted, some"] [299 3 "// old OpenSSL version will refuse to handshake if not present."] [300 3 "//"] [301 3 "// Per RFC 4492, section 5.1.2, implementations MUST support the"] [302 3 "// uncompressed point format. See golang.org/issue/31943."] [315 4 "// ML-DSA can only be used with TLS 1.3."] [337 1 "// negotiateALPN picks a shared ALPN protocol that both sides support in server"] [338 1 "// preference order. If ALPN is not configured or the peer doesn't support it,"] [339 1 "// it returns \"\" and no error."] [343 4 "// RFC 9001, Section 8.1"] [359 2 "// As a special case, let http/1.1 clients connect to h2 servers as if they"] [360 2 "// didn't support ALPN. We used not to enforce protocol overlap, so over"] [361 2 "// time a number of HTTP servers were configured with only \"h2\", but"] [362 2 "// expected to accept connections from \"http/1.1\" clients. See Issue 46310."] [369 1 "// supportsECDHE returns whether ECDHE key exchanges can be used with this"] [370 1 "// pre-TLS 1.3 client."] [389 2 "// Per RFC 8422, Section 5.1.2, if the Supported Point Formats extension is"] [390 2 "// missing, uncompressed points are supported. If supportedPoints is empty,"] [391 2 "// the extension must be missing, as an empty extension body is rejected by"] [392 2 "// the parser. See https://go.dev/issue/49126."] [417 4 "// The client is doing a fallback connection. See RFC 7507."] [430 29 "// arbace"] [453 1 "// checkForResumption reports whether we should perform resumption on this connection."] [483 2 "// TLS 1.2 tickets don't natively have a lifetime, but we want to avoid"] [484 2 "// re-wrapping the same master secret in different tickets over and over for"] [485 2 "// too long, weakening forward secrecy."] [491 2 "// Never resume a session for a different TLS version."] [497 2 "// Check that the client is still offering the ciphersuite in the session."] [508 2 "// Check that we also support the ciphersuite from the session."] [536 2 "// RFC 7627, Section 5.3"] [541 3 "// Aborting is somewhat harsh, but it's a MUST and it would indicate a"] [542 3 "// weird downgrade in client capabilities."] [547 4 "// FIPS 140-3 requires the use of Extended Master Secret."] [570 2 "// We echo the client's session ID in the ServerHello to let it know"] [571 2 "// that we're doing a resumption."] [573 2 "// We always send a new session ticket, even if it wraps the same master"] [574 2 "// secret and it's potentially encrypted with the same key, to help the"] [575 2 "// client avoid cross-connection tracking from a network observer."] [588 36 "// arbace"] [614 3 "// No need to keep a full record of the handshake if client"] [615 3 "// certificates won't be used."] [627 2 "// Set localCertificate here, rather than at certificate selection time, so"] [628 2 "// that it is only populated when a certificate is actually presented to the"] [629 2 "// peer, and not on resumed connections."] [661 3 "// Request a client certificate"] [672 3 "// An empty list of certificateAuthorities signals to"] [673 3 "// the client that it may send any certificate in response"] [674 3 "// to our request. When we know the CAs we trust, then"] [675 3 "// we can send them down, so that the client can choose"] [676 3 "// an appropriate certificate to give to us."] [694 27 "// public key for client auth, if any"] [701 2 "// If we requested a client certificate, then the client must send a"] [702 2 "// certificate message, even if it's empty."] [726 36 "// arbace"] [731 2 "// Get client key exchange"] [763 2 "// If we received a client cert in response to our certificate request message,"] [764 2 "// the client will send us a certificateVerifyMsg immediately after the"] [765 2 "// clientKeyExchangeMsg. This message is a digest of all preceding"] [766 2 "// handshake-layer messages that is signed using the private key corresponding"] [767 2 "// to the client's certificate. This allows us to verify that the client is in"] [768 2 "// possession of the private key of the certificate."] [770 3 "// certificateVerifyMsg is included in the transcript, but not until"] [771 3 "// after we verify the handshake signature, since the state before"] [772 3 "// this message was sent is used."] [795 21 "// ensure godebug is initialized"] [841 60 "/* for reading */"] [843 61 "/* not for reading */"] [863 2 "// finishedMsg is included in the transcript, but not until after we"] [864 2 "// check the client version, since the state before this message was"] [865 2 "// sent is used during verification."] [902 3 "// If this is re-wrapping an old key, then keep"] [903 3 "// the original time it was created."] [948 1 "// processCertsFromClient takes a chain of client certificates either from a"] [949 1 "// certificateMsg message or a certificateMsgTLS13 message and verifies them."] [951 72 "// arbace"] [954 1 "// processCertsFromClientAuth is processCertsFromClient under the clientAuth"] [955 1 "// policy (arbace: post-handshake authentication has its own)."] [1034 36 "// arbace"]] :go/pos {:name [5 9] :package [5 1]} :go/semis [[70 35] [76 35] [81 35] [84 31] [87 35] [90 49] [93 25] [97 33] [103 33] [106 31] [109 31] [112 49] [117 35] [120 33] [123 25] [170 61] [306 51] [324 54] [579 59] [582 68] [587 65] [618 59] [621 68] [631 67] [638 71] [650 59] [654 64] [680 68] [686 69] [690 24] [712 5] [725 65] [758 90] [802 107] [813 97] [821 56] [859 36] [883 59] [923 61] [933 39] [939 68] [961 53] [967 33] [997 62] [999 91] 